{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","is_bot":false,"login":"konard","name":"Konstantin Diachenko"},"baseRefName":"main","body":"## What\n- Adds a `/translate` library, CLI, HTTP, and web surface that formalizes text first, then translates resolved Wikidata Q/P phrases through target-language labels.\n- Extends `/formalize` with a CST rich enough to regenerate Markdown through `markdownFromFormalizationCst()`.\n- Preserves unresolved source terms as variables with generated questions, and exposes translation Markdown, HTML, Links Notation, and CST output.\n- Adds issue #16 case-study requirements, research notes, solution plan, captured GitHub/search data, and a web screenshot.\n\nFixes #16.\n\n## Screenshot\n![Translate page](https://github.com/link-assistant/meta-expression/blob/issue-16-a4cb3c8415b5/docs/case-studies/issue-16/translate-page.png?raw=true)\n\n## Reproduction\n- Before this change, `/formalize` results did not expose a reusable CST and there was no `/translate` API, CLI command, or web page that could translate formalized phrases.\n- `tests/issue-16.test.js` reproduces that missing behavior by asserting the formalization CST, Markdown regeneration, translation of `Hawaii` to Russian `Гавайи`, unresolved-variable questions, CLI parsing, async CLI output, HTTP `/translate`, and the static web translate page wiring.\n\n## Testing\n- `node --test tests/issue-16.test.js`\n- `deno test --allow-read tests/issue-16.test.js`\n- `deno test --allow-read`\n- `npm test`\n- `npm run check`\n- `scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `GITHUB_BASE_REF=main node scripts/validate-changeset.mjs`\n- Playwright smoke: `http://127.0.0.1:4173/web/#/translate`, `Hawaii` -> `Гавайи`","createdAt":"2026-05-08T19:19:22Z","headRefName":"issue-16-a4cb3c8415b5","headRefOid":"f8d10285a7cdeacb58dd82f66dbab22f2e809cd8","isDraft":true,"mergeable":"MERGEABLE","number":28,"reviewDecision":"","state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt